abstract: >-
  First-party engineering literature from SCITEO Advanced Materials (峻茂新材料), a manufacturer
  of advanced adhesives and polymer interface materials for semiconductor packaging and precision
  microelectronics. Seven product lines cover high-temperature adhesives, thermal interface materials,
  conductive adhesives, cryogenic adhesives, epoxy resins, semiconductor packaging adhesives and
  capillary underfill, serving semiconductor packaging, automotive electronics, extreme-temperature
  components and ultra-precision manufacturing. Catalog engineering envelope: temperature −255 °C to
  1000 °C; thermal conductivity 1.5–280 W/m·K (thermal adhesives and potting 1.5–60, sintered silver
  220–280); CTE 7.1–48 ppm/°C; Tg 90–280 °C; shear strength 5–32 MPa; volume resistivity
  3×10⁻⁶–10¹⁵ Ω·cm; cavity leak rate <1×10⁻⁸ atm·cc/s; CVCM <0.03% and TML <0.4% on cavity and
  optical grades. The 2026.11 release mirrors twenty-eight bilingual papers in fifty-six Markdown
  documents, rebuilt from the refactored site corpus. Coverage includes high-temperature failure
  physics from 200 to 1000 °C; thermal interface design at 100 W/cm² and 20–60 W/m·K; chip-grade
  conductive silver and pressureless sintered silver; die attach, wire-bond encapsulation and
  flip-chip underfill for CoWoS-L, HBM4 and glass substrates; temperature cycling and 85/85 damp-heat
  reliability with JEDEC, AEC-Q100 and GJB 150A test boundaries; accelerated life models; MEMS and
  CIS cavity sealing; low-temperature cure from 55 to 80 °C; cryogenic bonding from −55 to −255 °C;
  SMT defects on 008004 and SiP assemblies; high-density PCBA; PVD/CVD and wet-process masking;
  UV-cure active alignment; connector and harness potting; and module-level materials for humanoid
  joints, 1.6T optics and AI power. Each paper carries a citable TL;DR, key-facts table, Standards
  Reference block, FAQ appendix and a canonical link to the version of record on sciteo.com.
